<body>
    <h1>Meeting Minutes of 2026/07/06 - Demo Sharing</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p local-id=3D"9b7d31703f97">Hi all,</p>
<p local-id=3D"019d135dfe3b">Thank you all for attending this meeting. Belo=
w are the meeting minutes and future work arrangements.</p>
<p local-id=3D"c30c084856b4"></p>
<h3 local-id=3D"55b90c34f437" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/07/06-DemoSharing-=
QuickRecap"><strong>Quick Recap</strong></h3>
<p local-id=3D"3587f32df92a">This meeting is the third meeting of the =E6=
=B1=87=E4=B8=B0=E7=A7=91=E6=8A=80=E8=8F=81=E8=8B=B1=E8=AE=AD=E7=BB=83=E8=90=
=A5 =E2=80=93 AI=E6=99=BA=E8=83=BD=E9=97=AE=E7=AD=94=E5=8A=A9=E6=89=8B. The=
 session focused on two main topics: the progress of the AI project and pre=
parations for the upcoming demo on the 17th. Mu Guangyuan shared his resear=
ch on large model memory systems, including a three-module system based on =
the Lightman paper. Wang Yixi demonstrated the progress of the data pipelin=
e module, covering document conversion, chunking, and vector database stora=
ge. The team also discussed UI improvements, technical issues discovered du=
ring code integration, and the timeline for the demo PPT submission.</p>
<p local-id=3D"26d58d0f128a"></p>
<h3 local-id=3D"e48eda1cb8a2" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/07/06-DemoSharing-=
PlanSharing"><strong>Plan Sharing</strong></h3>
<p local-id=3D"01e0e123b6a0">Mu Guangyuan: Shared his research on optimizin=
g large model memory systems. He introduced a cost-effective three-module s=
ystem (information filtering, topic segmentation, and compression) based on=
 the Lightman paper. The system uses small models for information extractio=
n and an attention-based mechanism for topic block segmentation, featuring =
an innovative "artificial sleep" update mechanism for memory optimization. =
He also introduced a pluggable memory system as a lightweight external memo=
ry maintenance plugin applicable to various projects.</p>
<p local-id=3D"0e99d44210ba">Wang Yixi: Demonstrated the progress of the da=
ta pipeline module. The current test version (without large model integrati=
on) can convert documents into a unified document model and process queries=
 with relevant information and relevance scores. She also shared several te=
chnical issues discovered during code integration, including inconsistent P=
DF parsing results, code structure optimization suggestions, and interface =
adapter implementation.</p>
<p local-id=3D"ea5925b46efd">Vincent: Proposed multiple UI improvements, in=
cluding page layout optimization, adding statistical data displays (e.g., h=
it count, total count), modifying the logo, and adding a high-level archite=
cture diagram for the PPT. He emphasized that UI design is critical for the=
 judges' impression during the demo. He also confirmed the timeline for the=
 PPT draft submission next Thursday and discussed the allocation of the 8-m=
inute presentation time.</p>
<p local-id=3D"96ebe7229a2b"></p>
<h3 local-id=3D"51a2cebb4951" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/07/06-DemoSharing-=
DiscussionSummary"><strong>Discussion Summary</strong></h3>
<p local-id=3D"0d607578c8de">-UI Improvements: The team agreed to optimize =
the front-end display page by removing unnecessary buttons, adjusting resul=
t presentation (e.g., tree structure, highlighting key information), adding=
 statistics, and changing the top-left icon to the project or AI name. Vinc=
ent suggested using an AI-generated logo.</p>
<p local-id=3D"331222359913">PDF Parsing Issues:The team acknowledged the l=
imitations of PDF parsing due to its nature as a print-oriented format. Con=
sensus was reached to prioritize structured file formats such as Word, Exce=
l, and HTML, and to lower the priority of PDF optimization unless it become=
s a significant requirement during future integration with other project gr=
oups.</p>
<p local-id=3D"03dea695967d">Code Structure Optimization: The team agreed t=
o clean up test and redundant code (e.g., local JSON search, evaluation mod=
ules) to avoid mixing with core functionality, ensuring clear and maintaina=
ble code.</p>
<p local-id=3D"47bdd88b463b">Demo Preparation: The team confirmed that Wang=
 Yixi will prepare the first draft of the PPT by Thursday, with a total pre=
sentation time of 8 minutes covering both the demo and PPT explanation.</p>
<p local-id=3D"552b926eae8f"></p>
<h3 local-id=3D"410cc88f0da6" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/07/06-DemoSharing-=
ActionItems"><strong>Action Items</strong></h3>
<p local-id=3D"dee75afaa776"><strong>Vincent</strong>=EF=BC=9AFollow up wit=
h large model resource providers this week to obtain available APIs or API =
keys for project integration. |</p>
<p local-id=3D"2013f34ce552"><strong>Wang Yixi</strong>=EF=BC=9AOptimize th=
e front-end display page before the 17th (remove unnecessary buttons, adjus=
t result display with tree structure and key information highlights, add st=
atistics such as hit count and total count, change the top-left icon to the=
 project or AI name, and prepare a high-level architecture diagram for the =
PPT). |</p>
<p local-id=3D"b6b39a151a30"><strong>Project Team</strong>=EF=BC=9AWhen int=
egrating with other project groups (e.g., conference-related), reassess whe=
ther PDF parsing optimization is needed if the proportion of PDF files is h=
igh; currently lower the priority of PDF parsing and focus on structured fi=
le formats like Word, Excel, and HTML.&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"626db3f255f0">Project Team=EF=BC=9AReview and optimize code =
structure, remove test or redundant code (e.g., local JSON search, evaluati=
on test modules) to avoid mixing with core functions, ensuring clear and ma=
intainable code.</p>
<p local-id=3D"8f8d57acd72a"></p>
<p local-id=3D"db6cbe08ef4d">Kind regards,</p>
<p local-id=3D"72e96ea319d3">Yixi Wang</p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
